Emoji artwork

  The SVG files are from Google's Noto Emoji,
  https://github.com/googlefonts/noto-emoji, folder 2D/svg, at the commit
  named in UPSTREAM_COMMIT.txt. Copyright 2013 Google, Inc. Licensed under
  the Apache License, Version 2.0; LICENSE-noto-emoji.txt has the notice of
  that folder (2D/svg/LICENSE) and the text of the license.

  The country and subdivision flags are from the same repository, folder
  third_party/region-flags/waved-svg (the waved flags of the Noto Color
  Emoji font). Their designs are in the public domain or otherwise exempt
  from copyright; LICENSE-noto-emoji.txt ends with that folder's license
  (third_party/region-flags/LICENSE).

  What EmOji-san changed (Apache License 2.0, section 4b):
  - It includes part of the files. Skin-tone variants are left out.
  - It renamed the files from code points (emoji_u1f3ea.svg) to names
    (convenience_store.svg) and sorted them into one folder per category.
  - It rewrote the files that Qt, which draws the markers in QGIS, gets
    wrong: those with clip paths, with a gradient that refers to another
    gradient, or with rgba() colors. picosvg
    (https://github.com/googlefonts/picosvg) applies the clip paths to the
    shapes and resolves the references; rgba() colors become a color and an
    opacity. The picture stays the same. Each of these files says in a
    comment at its top that it was changed.
  - It did not change the content of the other SVG files.

